---
const title = "Now";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="What earthlingmaeve is currently learning and building."
    />
    <title>{title} | earthlingmaeve</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header>
      <nav>
        <a href="/" class="logo">earthlingmaeve</a>

        <div class="nav-links">
          <a href="/#projects">Projects</a>
          <a href="/#blog">Blog</a>
          <a href="/now">Now</a>
          <a href="/#about">About</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/earthlingmaeve">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main>
      <p class="eyebrow">NOW</p>

      <h1>What I'm working on</h1>

      <p class="intro">
        A snapshot of what I'm currently learning, building, and
        experimenting with.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>Building</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Active Directory IAM Lab</strong> — building an
            enterprise-style identity environment from the ground up.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Portfolio</strong> — documenting the work with Astro,
            GitHub, and GitHub Pages.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Learning</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>Active Directory and Windows identity</li>
          <li>Group Policy and access control</li>
          <li>PowerShell automation</li>
          <li>IAM lifecycle management</li>
          <li>Microsoft Entra ID</li>
          <li>Cloud identity and Azure RBAC</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Next up</h2>

        <p>
          Build the fictional organization for the AD lab, design the
          organizational-unit structure, create role-based groups, and
          start documenting the identity model.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Why a Now page?</h2>

        <p>
          This page is intentionally more temporary than the rest of the
          site. Projects describe what I've built; this page describes
          what I'm focused on right now.
        </p>

        <p>
          I'll update it as the focus of the homelab changes.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <p>Built with Astro · Documented on GitHub</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(*) {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    font-family:
      Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont,
      "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #172033;
    background: #f7f8fa;
  }

  :global(a) {
    color: inherit;
  }

  header {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e5ea;
  }

  nav {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .logo {
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .nav-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .nav-links a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  main {
    max-width: 850px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 5rem 1.5rem 6rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: #596579;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 5rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-size: 2rem;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: #596579;
  }

  section {
    padding: 3.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e5ea;
  }

  li {
    margin: 0.6rem 0;
  }

  footer {
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1.5rem;
    color: #596579;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    nav {
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
